  "worked_solution": "The angles ${30}^{∘}$ and ${60}^{∘}$ are special, and their trigonometric ratios have the  values\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘} & = \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & = \\\\ 0 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
